**Detection Strategies for CVE-2015-0311:**

**Network Level:**
- Monitor for unusually large compressed payloads
- Alert on malformed zlib headers (magic bytes 0x78 0x9C/0xDA)
- Track compression ratio anomalies (compression bombs)

**Application Level:**
- Log all uncompress() operations with size before/after
- Set maximum decompressed size limits
- Implement try-catch with detailed error logging

**System Level:**
- Enable crash dump collection
- Monitor for Flash Player crashes
- Use EMET/Exploit Guard for DEP/ASLR enforcement

**Example Logging:**
```actionscript
try {
    var originalSize:int = mainBuffer.length;
    mainBuffer.uncompress();
    var decompressedSize:int = mainBuffer.length;
    log("Decompress: " + originalSize + " -> " + decompressedSize);
    if (decompressedSize > MAX_SAFE_SIZE) {
        throw new Error("Decompression bomb detected");
    }
} catch (e:Error) {
    log("ALERT: Decompression failed - possible exploit attempt");
}
```

